WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
A sharp mosaic from the lunar reconnaissance orbiter shows the moon's far side has a thicker crust that prevents dark maria from forming. This is Fascinating Frontiers, Episode 218. The lunar reconnaissance orbiter wide-angle camera gathered the data for this full hemisphere view. The composite draws on more than 15,000 separate frames taken between November 2009 and February 2011. At its sharpest, the map resolves features down to 100 meters per pixel. The far side surface appears heavily cratered

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.860
and lacks the broad dark planes that mark the near side.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.200
A thicker crust on that side appears to block molten rock

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.760
from reaching the surface and forming smooth maria.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:42.220
No Earth-based images contributed to the final product.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.740
The moon measures roughly one quarter the diameter of Earth,

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:48.420
yet its two hemispheres differ sharply in appearance.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:51.240
One side carries extensive dark planes

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.180
while the other remains a continuous stretch

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:54.460
of lighter cratered terrain.

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:58.200
The far side crust sits several kilometers deeper on average.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:03.100
That added depth keeps interior melt from breaking through and resurfacing the landscape.

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:08.940
The orbiter built the elevation map by counting craters and measuring heights at 100m resolution.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:14.040
The resulting surface preserves 4 billion years of impact history without later volcanic

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:14.640
resets.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:19.440
Researchers still lack a clear explanation for why one side developed the thicker crust

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:20.240
in the first place.

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:25.300
Next we turn to a new infrared survey that is cataloging objects cooler than stars.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:30.620
NASA's Fieryx Space Telescope has begun mapping brown dwarfs whose atmospheres contain

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:31.600
water and methane.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:36.040
The survey reaches objects too faint for earlier instruments to study in detail.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:41.380
Systematic observations now let astronomers compare atmospheric chemistry across a wide

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:42.840
range of temperatures and ages.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:47.360
Published results in the astrophysical journal highlight the chemical similarity to

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:49.300
giant planets in our own solar system.

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:54.040
One remaining question centers on whether free floating planets share the same atmospheric

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:59.140
The telescope has already added dozens of new targets suitable for follow-up spectroscopy.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:04.580
The James Webb Space Telescope used infrared light to pier through dust in a nebula

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:06.680
and revealed many stars of different ages.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.500
This helps study how stars change over time.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:12.960
The observations penetrate regions opaque to visible light.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:16.460
Multiple generations of stars appear in the same field of view.

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:19.380
While Sphere X examines these cool atmospheres,

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:23.240
another observatory is turning its attention to the end stages of stellar life.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:27.680
NASA has issued a request for proposals seeking commercial space stations to

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:32.380
succeed the International Space Station as early as 2030. Responses must

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:36.860
arrive by December 8th. The agency expects to select two or more contractors

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:41.060
with a final decision set for April. Phase one winners will receive at least

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:46.420
$100 million each. Axiom Space, Voyager Space, and Vass Space have already

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:51.400
signaled interest. The solicitation document runs 360 pages and spells out

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:56.520
required station capabilities. Later phases will fund development certification and at least

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:02.300
four crude missions. Northrop Grumman's Cygnus XL spacecraft has now undocked from the International

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:08.120
Space Station after a six-month stay. The vehicle delivered more than 11,000 pounds of supplies

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:13.380
and experiments during its time docked. It also carried experimental heat shield capsules intended

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:18.800
for reentry testing. This flight marked the company's 24th cargo resupply mission for NASA.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:23.740
The capsules will evaluate next-generation thermal protection materials during their return.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:34.060
The James Webb Space Telescope has captured a striking gravitational lens created by the Galaxy cluster MACS J0454.1-0300.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:39.620
Background galaxies appear warped and multiplied into multiple images of the same objects.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:43.380
Light from those distant sources bends around the foreground cluster.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:47.980
The effect magnifies faint galaxies that would otherwise remain undetectable.

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:52.540
The cluster therefore functions as a natural telescope extending Web's reach.

00:03:53.160 --> 00:04:01.560
Observations of the coldest known brown dwarf Y0855 have revealed variable water clouds outside the solar system for the first time.

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:07.500
Web monitored the Jupiter-sized object for 11 hours at a distance of 7.5 light years.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:12.140
Spectra collected every 15 minutes showed the clouds changing over that period.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:17.140
The detection marks the first confirmed case of variable water clouds beyond our planetary

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:17.780
system.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:23.200
Analysis of white dwarf stars suggests strong magnetic fields may allow some remnants to

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.880
exceed the usual 1.4 solar mass limit.

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:31.060
The standard Chandrasek R limit applies to non-rotating non-magnetized objects.

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:36.000
Magnetic support could therefore change the final evolutionary path for certain stars.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:43.080
The profile of engineer Robert Zubrin in the October 9, 2026 issue of the economist traces

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:46.240
how his Mars mission concepts influenced later plans.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:51.160
Zubrin developed detailed engineering proposals for crude journeys over several decades.

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:56.600
Geneva has been chosen to host the 2029 International Astronautical Congress.

00:04:57.140 --> 00:05:01.940
The Swiss city defeated bids from Houston and Barcelona during the vote in Antalya, Turkey.

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:07.800
Swiss Mem and the Swiss Space Office led the winning proposal for the 80th edition of the annual gathering.

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:13.680
Astronaut Kelly Girardi is preparing for a commercial space flight while balancing family responsibilities.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:17.660
Her training includes weightlessness, preparation, and safety procedures.

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:22.100
The experience also requires psychological readiness for periods of isolation.

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:28.160
An amateur astronomer has used the AI tool Claude to identify a potential new planet candidate.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:31.740
The initial detection required no professional telescope time.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:36.800
The case raises questions about how such tools might assist future observational work.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:40.920
Carl Schwartzchild was born on October 9, 1873.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:46.000
He published a paper on celestial mechanics at age 16 while studying at the University

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:46.740
of Strasbourg.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:51.460
His later contributions advance both general relativity and black hole theory.

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:56.480
The Copernicus Sentinel-2 mission acquired an image of a Tosha National Park in northern

00:05:56.480 --> 00:06:03.560
Namibia on April 5, 2026. It captures the country's biggest salt pan. The salt pan appears as a

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:09.440
bright, flat expanse amid surrounding terrain. Sentinel-2 provides multispectral data useful for

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:14.540
monitoring erud regions. The acquisition date falls during the dry season when surface features

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:20.440
stand out clearly. President Trump awarded Elon Musk the National Medal of Science. The award

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:26.040
recognizes Musk's contributions through SpaceX. It highlights ongoing private sector involvement

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:31.540
in space exploration. The metal acknowledges engineering achievements in reusable launch systems.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:37.100
SpaceX operations have expanded access to orbit for both government and commercial payloads.

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:42.120
Before we go, keep an eye on the next round of commercial station proposals that close in December.

